INT. COUNTY COURTHOUSE, SMALL CLAIMS - DAY

Fluorescent lights. A radiator knocking. Four chairs and a table.

A MAN in a rumpled tan jacket sits alone at the defendant's table, studying his own thumbs.

JUDGE PRISCILLA OYELOWO-HART (60s) enters, sits, and bangs the gavel once.

JUDGE
We're on the record. Counsel for the plaintiff?

FELIPE ARRIAGA (30s, bright tie) rises.

FELIPE
Felipe Arriaga, Your Honor.

JUDGE
And the defendant?

MAN
Just me, ma'am.

JUDGE
Name for the record.

MAN
Dutch Halloran.

JUDGE
Mr. Halloran, you're unrepresented?

DUTCH
Yes, ma'am. I figured the truth doesn't need a lawyer.

JUDGE
It usually needs one.

At the back of the room, CLERK BARNABY SKOLNICK (50s) stifles a laugh. Felipe sits and Dutch rises at the same moment.

FELIPE
Your Honor, my client withdraws the claim.

DUTCH ^
Your Honor, I'd like to pay it.

The Judge looks from one to the other. She sighs and lowers the gavel.

JUDGE
Nobody leaves until I understand why.
